<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 2172) <span class="when">Nov 6, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Menus sorted by what you're doing,</b> each group under a small heading.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 2165) <span class="when">Nov 6, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixes and improvements</b> shared with Asobi.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2162) <span class="when">Nov 5, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixes and improvements</b> shared with Asobi.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2152) <span class="when">Nov 5, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Report a problem from Asobi Review.</b> Help ▸ Report a Problem… makes a report with pictures, a voice note or a short recording, ready to send to us.</li>
<li><b>Resync.</b> Review ▸ Resync takes you back to where the host is.</li>
<li><b>New clips arrive by themselves.</b> When the room goes to a clip that is still on its way, Asobi Review says so and goes to it when it's ready.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2140) <span class="when">Nov 5, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Catch Up with the Room.</b> Review ▸ Catch Up with the Room (or a right-click on the Live chip) takes you to the host's clip and frame at once.</li>
<li><b>Reviews stay in step.</b> If your Mac ends up on another clip or frame than the host's, it goes back by itself within a few seconds.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2136) <span class="when">Nov 4, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Kitsu playlists play the version they name,</b> even when two of a shot's tasks have the same version number.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2132) <span class="when">Nov 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Improvements and fixes.</b></li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2128) <span class="when">Nov 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Quitting no longer crashes</b> while EXR frames are still being read.</li>
<li><b>Improvements and fixes.</b></li>
</ul>
]]></description>
